	spec: 'In the terminal, a batch of parallel tool calls shows each result right under its own call, as one card, as web cards do; each call streams under its own header and keeps its output when done. Exception (terminal only; the web has no immutable scrollback): when the batch drawn grouped (measured rows; a call still waiting counts a one-row result) is taller than the screen, calls and results stay separate blocks and each result links to its call (#<call>), so a finishing call never rewrites scrollback. A batch that once overflowed stays split; its layout never flips back. Display order only (frame.order); the transcript keeps arrival order. Background bash output arrives later as its own block. Invariant restored: three parallel inspect calls showed three headers, then three detached results.',
